  "limitations": [
    "This is an aggregate type, shape, cardinality, and version census of five bounded sources. It does not resolve people, authenticate companies or customers, establish a tenant bridge, or identify Hong Kong entities or current activity.",
    "Rows, decoded-record versions, raw-line versions, surrogate string groups, and array elements are different units. Source totals must not be interpreted as unique companies, people, tenants, or resources.",
    "Equality and cardinality use source-and-field-qualified typed hashes privately. No cross-source equality bridge is computed. Raw values, identifiers, names, field-name hashes, and value hashes are excluded from this artifact.",
    "Multiple whole-record versions within a surrogate string group are not automatically conflicts. They may reflect identity-model multiplicity; no latest version or historical validity is elected.",
    "All enum meanings remain unreviewed. A decimal, hexadecimal, or UUID-shaped string is a syntax observation, not an admitted identifier namespace or evidence of a corporate identity.",
    "Every tenant-array element was typed. Source-local surrogate/array-set counts do not authenticate native tenant ownership or establish a relationship between datasets.",
    "The dated finance bootstrap source remains separate from the registry. Similar counts or shapes do not establish equal source content, equivalence, or compatible mappings.",
    "Timestamp categories describe parseability only. Unsupported timestamps do not establish current or historical states; first-seen, last-seen, bootstrap, and creation fields are not proven effective dates.",
    "Additional top-level keys absent from the sampled schema are counted by source only. Their names and contents remain outside the admitted field scope.",
    "Billing-capability flags and model names are source categories, not proof of payment, product use, incident impact, or customer status. Further interpretation requires transformation lineage, enum dictionaries, namespace/key constraints, and effective-date policies."
  ]
}
